"v":0.0},{"s":2009,"v":0.0},{"s":2010,"v":0.0},{"s":2011,"v":0.0},{"s":2012,"v":0.0},{"s":2013,"v":0.0},{"s":2014,"v":0.0},{"s":2015,"v":0.0},{"s":2016,"v":0.0},{"s":2017,"v":0.1},{"s":2018,"v":0.0},{"s":2019,"v":0.0},{"s":2020,"v":0.0},{"s":2021,"v":0.0},{"s":2022,"v":0.0},{"s":2023,"v":0.0},{"s":2024,"v":1.9},{"s":2025,"v":0.0}],"t_snow":{"per_decade":-0.003,"lo":-0.044,"hi":0.038,"class":"noise","n":71,"first":1943,"last":2025,"intercept":0.6786048358569693,"slope":-0.00029382779261999815,"total":-0.0},"snow_normal":0.0},"titles":{"year":"2026 so far: 8 daily record highs, 2 daily record lows","records":"Tallahassee is setting record highs far faster than chance","change":"Tallahassee's nights cooled over the long run but have warmed since 1986. Its days have warmed.","rain":"Rain: no clear long-term change"},"text":{"lede":"Yesterday's high of 68\u00b0F was typical for November 13.","t_yest":"November 13 was a typical day","p_yest":"The high of <strong>68\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13. The normal high for the date is 73\u00b0F, and the record is 86\u00b0F (1915). The low of <strong>41\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Tallahassee is setting record highs far faster than chance","p_rec":"If Tallahassee's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Tallahassee has set <strong>53 standing record lows</strong>, fewer than the 74 that chance alone would give, and <strong class=\"sig\">137 record highs</strong>, far more than the 74 that chance alone would give. The 2010s hold the most record highs of any decade (63). Tallahassee's all-time high is 105\u00b0F, on June 15, 2011.","t_chg":"Tallahassee's nights cooled over the long run but have warmed since 1986. Its days have warmed.","p_chg":"Across 126 complete years: Tallahassee's average low has fallen <strong class='sig'>\u22120.12\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range \u22120.20 to \u22120.04), about \u22121.6\u00b0F since 1893. Tallahassee's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.28\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.21 to +0.34), about +3.6\u00b0F since 1893. <strong>The last 40 years tell a different story:</strong> since 1986, lows have risen <strong class='sig'>+1.09\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.73 to +1.46) and highs have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.49\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.19 to +0.79). The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 2 of 12 months; 6 months fell. Highs rose in 11 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Tallahassee's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.30 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 58.8 inches a year. The wettest year was 1964 (104.18 in); the driest, 1954 (30.98 in). Tallahassee almost never sees snow (the 1991\u20132020 average is 0.0 inches a winter), so there's no snowfall chart.","show_snow":false,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":true},"t_year":"2026 so far: 8 daily record highs, 2 daily record lows"}}